// ULTRAKILL 1-4: CLAIR DE LUNE - "double_dead", brutal.
// Converted from double_dead.lua (UNItas style Lua) into UKTAS framebulks.
//
// HOW THE INPUT WAS TRANSLATED
//   movie.frame_advance(n)        -> a framebulk of n ticks
//   key.hold(x) .. 1 advance .. release -> x pressed for exactly one tick
//   mouse.left / mouse.right      -> 1 (primary fire) / 2 (alt fire)
//   angle(yaw, pitch)             -> d+<yaw> / d+<pitch> on the tick it landed on
//                                    (pitch is positive DOWN in both tools)
//   equipWeapon("Alpha5")         -> -----w5 ...
//   equipVariant(...)             -> y1/y2/y3 (blue/green/red), see the note below
//   left ctrl / left shift / W A S D / space -> s d f l r b j in the movement field
//   key.hold("Q")                 -> v (whiplash)      key.hold("F") -> F (feedbacker punch)
//   key.hold("C")                 -> K (knuckleblaster punch)
//   key.hold("G")                 -> x (change fist)
//   "right shift" (its "Tab Menu") -> S (stats overlay), two presses as in the original
//   env.fps = 200 / 140 / 120     -> host_frametime 0.005, with per-line frametime
//                                    0.007142857... and 0.008333333... for the two slows
//
// TWO DELIBERATE CHANGES
//  1. Variant selection. The Lua pressed the keys "E", "R" and "T" (the author had them
//     bound to variation slots) and its prints name the variant each press was meant to
//     pick. This file uses explicit variation slots instead, so the result never depends
//     on which variant happened to be equipped before:
//         y1 = blue   y2 = green   y3 = red
//     As used here:  Freezeframe y1, S.R.S. Cannon y2, Firestarter y3,
//                    Core Eject y1, Sawed-On y3, Marksman y2.
//     The original's prints say "S.R.S. Cannon" and "Core Eject Hammer" in a few places
//     where it did NOT press a variant key (it relied on whatever was already out). Those
//     lines are kept exactly as the original had them - see the comments there if the run
//     needs the blue shotgun / green rocket for that trick.
//  2. The title-screen and level-select clicks (mouse.move to 440,630 / 320,460 /
//     960,680 / 1595,660 at 1920x1080) are replaced by the header's level load, so the
//     difficulty is set by `difficulty brutal` and not by a menu click. The original's
//     menu section, kept for reference:
//         advance 6, escape, advance 1, advance 60
//         mouse 440,630 click (5 ticks), advance 150
//         mouse 320,460 (5) click (5) - its print says VIOLENT; a click here overrides
//         the header difficulty
//         advance 100, mouse 960,680 (5) click (5), advance 40
//         mouse 1595,660 click (5), advance 60
//     Everything from the first tick after control here is the original's tick sequence:
//     60 settle ticks, its two "Tab Menu" presses, then 250 ticks before the first equip.
//     If the opening desyncs, tune those counts - they were measured in the other tool.
//
// NEEDS: rocket launcher (Freezeframe + Firestarter at least), shotgun (Core Eject +
// Sawed-On), revolver (Marksman), railcannon set to Malicious, knuckleblaster owned.
version 1
host_frametime 0.005
seed 1337
start_type load_level 1-4
difficulty brutal
wait_for_control true
fist parry
frames

// ============================ LEVEL START ==================================
